WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:04.870
Install Contract Intelligence & Register
in your own Microsoft environment.

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.730
With the prerequisites already in place,
allow roughly 20 to 30 minutes for setup.

3
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.250
This is a planning estimate, not
a measured installation time.

4
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.640
Preparing permissions or capacity
may take additional time.

5
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.420
Keep INSTALL.pdf open for
the detailed instructions.

6
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.326
First, check that you have a Dataverse
environment with at least 1 GB free,

7
00:00:25.326 --> 00:00:28.960
System Administrator access
and Copilot Studio capacity.

8
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.970
You also need a dedicated
SharePoint contract library,

9
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.600
a reviewer and alert
administrator with Teams,

10
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.810
Microsoft 365 admin access and a
text-based English contract for testing.

11
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.040
Microsoft usage charges are
separate from your licence.

12
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.280
Before uploading contracts,
configure capacity

13
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.410
and budget alerts at
50, 80 and 100 per cent.

14
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.490
Budget alerts do not stop spending.

15
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:56.070
Next, download your bundle and verify
its checksum against your order page.

16
00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.000
Extract the outer bundle, but leave the
managed solution ZIP inside it unopened.

17
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.902
Have five values ready: your SharePoint
site address, contract library ID,

18
00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:10.370
reviewer email, alert administrator
email and exact owner team name.

19
00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.160
The guide shows where to find them.

20
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.160
Open make.powerapps.com and
select your environment.

21
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.220
Choose Solutions, then Import solution,
and select the managed solution ZIP.

22
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.900
Connect both Dataverse references
to the same Dataverse connection.

23
00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.080
Also connect SharePoint and Teams.

24
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.790
Use the same System Administrator
account for all four references.

25
00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.960
Enter your five values and import.

26
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.450
If Import stays grey,
re-enter each required value.

27
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:42.470
After import, open Agents, All agents
in the Microsoft 365 admin centre.

28
00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.300
Check CAI Contract Intelligence Assistant.

29
00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.620
If its status is Available, block it.

30
00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.050
Leave it Draft or Blocked during setup.

31
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.770
Now check the solution's
seven cloud flows.

32
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.052
Turn on the required flows,
especially Review gate,

33
00:01:56.052 --> 00:01:58.340
which sends approval cards to Teams.

34
00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.680
Keep Daily recompute off during testing.

35
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.920
It consumes capacity when enabled.

36
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.280
Create the owner team using
exactly the name you entered.

37
00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.310
Assign CAI Contract Reader
and add the permitted users.

38
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.197
Check the role against the guide:
Read on Contract and Field evidence,

39
00:02:14.197 --> 00:02:17.220
with no additional permissions
specified for this role.

40
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:22.197
In Copilot Studio, check four settings:
no connected channel, sharing restricted

41
00:02:22.197 --> 00:02:27.010
to the owner, Authenticate with Microsoft
selected, and both topics turned on.

42
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.120
Do not publish the agent
during installation.

43
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.490
You can also run the
included readiness check.

44
00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.790
It changes nothing; the
final result should be READY.

45
00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.440
Finally, test with an owner-team account.

46
00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.600
Upload your test contract and wait for
Pending review and the Teams review card.

47
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.110
Approve the contract.

48
00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.433
In the Copilot Studio test pane, ask:

49
00:02:45.433 --> 00:02:48.580
“Which notice deadlines
fall in the next 400 days?”

50
00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.005
Allow the connection if
prompted, and check that

51
00:02:51.005 --> 00:02:53.540
the answer contains your
team's approved contracts.

52
00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.783
Before approving real contracts,
reviewers should read section 9a of

53
00:02:57.783 --> 00:03:01.800
INSTALL.pdf and check notice
periods against the source contract.

54
00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:08.700
For help, contact hello@colleagueai.ai
with your order email and release number.
